From: mscharged-port native source preparation
Subject: [PATCH] Deliver true native VI interrupts outside graphics output waits
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

Separate true VI field clock/cause and source interrupt delivery from native
output servicing. Keep a distinct output lifetime/nonreentry guard so actual
owner safe points can deliver pending fields during a GPU/window wait.
Use this IRQ-only composition at the existing completed-MCU and one-millisecond
FIFO/render-worker safe points. Actual masks, source callbacks and latched
cause behavior remain authoritative; no missed callback sequence is replayed.
Source callbacks retain their own behavior. Current movie callback closure is
qualified separately from future source loading-indicator graphics callbacks.
No game algorithm, playback decision, decoder equation or completion changes.

